{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ReactorRouter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ReactorRouter"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13ReactorRouterV"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ReactorRouter"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registered for three events opens with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"event.event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not — it is the ","type":"text"},{"code":"default:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arm that returns ","type":"text"},{"code":".allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on behalf of code that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rule does not reach it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reactor handler is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure, and collecting ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" members by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at compile time, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trade for the same reason.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"PURE SUGAR.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signs no reply and interprets no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout_ms"},{"type":"text","text":"; its output is exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/init()"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/boundEvents"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/fallback(_: